        "display": "Subtask complete. All five tests pass with exit code 0.\n\n**What was done:**\n- Read existing files first: `lru-cache.cjs` was a stub (`// Fixed incomplete LRU fixture. module.exports = {};`), and `lru-cache.test.cjs` was preserved unchanged (read receipt `read:986be1d5...`).\n- Implemented `lru-cache.cjs` as CommonJS exporting `class LRUCache`:\n  - `constructor(capacity, ttlMs = Infinity)`.\n  - `get(key)` returns the value or `undefined`; expired entries are removed and return `undefined`; live entries are refreshed to most-recently-used via Map delete+reinsert.\n  - `set(key, value)` inserts or updates (updates refresh recency and don't count against capacity); when capacity is exceeded, evicts the least-recently-used key (first key in Map order). TTL is reset from each set's time.\n  - `delete(key)` returns whether the key existed.\n- Applied via `workspace_apply` (receipt `batch:8b836e76...`, written version sha256 `9b7abc67836da914323132eab66df08289e2c20ca49c29076688450c375d7491`, 1066 bytes).\n- Captured resulting manifest and ran managed Node: `workspace_run` argv `[\"--test\",\"--test-reporter=tap\",\"@input/lru-cache.test.cjs\"]` against `manifest:0cc55db4...` → receipt `run:6d6b21ac...`, `exitCode: 0`.\n\n**Test evidence (TAP output, actual):**\n```\n# tests 5\n# pass 5\n# fail 0\nok 1 - missing keys return undefined\nok 2 - get refreshes recency and capacity evicts oldest\nok 3 - updating a key preserves capacity\nok 4 - delete removes only the chosen key\nok 5 - optional TTL expires entries\n```\n\n**Files:** `lru-cache.cjs` (implemented, sha256 `9b7abc67...`) and `lru-cache.test.cjs` (unchanged, sha256 `0336e968...`). No tests were modified; no receipts were invented.",
